   "body": "**Capture skipped (mac/capture-batch, batch 3, 2026-11-02): no traceable REST request to record.**\n\n- Legacy never calls a Giphy REST endpoint: it embeds the binary GiphyUISDK and configures it with an SDK key (`HFRswift/Swift/HFRswiftApp.swift:20`, `Classes/AddMessageViewController.m:154`, picker `AnswerView.swift`). No Giphy URL, query or response shape appears in the legacy code, the specs or the corpus, so a `search`/`trending` request would be written from Giphy's public docs, not from a trace (LESSONS 35-36).\n- ADR 0007 says the legacy key values are reused, but this Mac has no local untracked configuration holding a Giphy key, and the legacy key is an **SDK** key: whether it may (or can) be used against the REST API is the key owner's call.\n\nOptions:\n1. The operator provides a REST API key in the untracked local config (ADR 0007) and accepts the REST endpoints of Giphy's public API reference as the source for LOT-098 (#190); the next capture session records one `search` and one `trending` (rating R), key stripped.\n2. LOT-098 records the SDK's traffic instead (proxy on the Mac), which still needs the key and a decision on the SDK.\n3. Drop the GIF picker (ADR 0007 \"Alternatives\").\n\nReleased; labelled `status: blocked` until then. Decision needed (operator)\n",
   "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
